        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-18T18:11:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t know about IsReplacedByPrebuilt(). That does make it simpler.\n\nIt certainly makes sense to ignore disabled modules.\n\nIt seems to me that when deciding between whether the prebuilt or source modules should be used it is better to use the explicit and specific methods that indicate which of them should be preferred than something like IsHideFromMake() which is more general state and is used for a number of different reasons.\n\nI haven\u0027t debugged the test to check why both the source and prebuilt are hidden for make but it does seem to indicate that hidden for make is not the correct check.",
      "parentUuid": "b0acfb88_cec1fe66",
      "revId": "720ed452346bc92bd82e3d3c1c6def453e1928d6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
